**Amendment (Compact full-content representation)** · `amend:observe:compact-content` Refines (`amend:observe:full-content`) without changing the public-content boundary. Public byte values use a tagged UTF-8 JSON string when valid, otherwise padded RFC 4648 base64, with their byte length. Available structural Debug carriers are decoded into tagged JSON constructors, fields, sequences and literals; custom formatting outside that grammar remains explicitly identified available text rather than guessed fields or an invented serialization contract. Opaque capabilities retain their declared unavailable representation. Payload children are addressed before envelopes, so changing timestamps or totals does not duplicate their stored content. A complete JSON field exceeding {{ numval('num:numbers:observe-inline-byte-threshold') }} encoded bytes is stored once by SHA-256 content address, with digest, original encoded length and path replacing the inline representation; existing content is verified and atomic publication never overwrites an object. The default command store is .lane/observations/objects/sha256 beneath its working directory, overridden by PN_OBSERVE_ARTIFACT_DIR; the gate explicitly selects its checkout's .lane/observations. Artifact I/O runs on the delivery worker. Complete delivered records remain below {{ numval('num:numbers:observe-record-byte-capacity') }} bytes; a larger envelope is itself addressed. Queue admission is bounded by {{ numval('num:numbers:observe-historical-queue-record-capacity') }} records and {{ numval('num:numbers:observe-queued-byte-capacity') }} bytes of captured serialized bytes, with {{ numval('num:numbers:observe-reserved-summary-slot-count') }} reserved summary slots of {{ numval('num:numbers:observe-record-byte-capacity') }} bytes, {{ numval('num:numbers:observe-reserved-diagnostic-slot-count') }} diagnostic slots of {{ numval('num:numbers:observe-record-byte-capacity') }} bytes and one independent drain request; terminal records are serviced before ordinary backlog and queue saturation cannot reject the drain immediately; capacity, unavailable storage and disconnected delivery count whole-observation loss under (`rule:observe:sampling`), never field filtering or binding failure. The default gate keeps its observation records inline; explicit traced-run streams can be separated with ci/observation_log.py without changing their bytes. Structural value traits inherit the consuming operation so hashing, comparison, clone and teardown do not repeatedly record the same whole value.

**Amendment (Independent resource qualification)** · `amend:observe:resource-qualification` Implements the independent qualification promised by (`amend:observe:core-accounting`): resources accepts separate current and cumulative accuracy arguments. An unavailable current reading becomes null while retaining the previously observed high-water value and its accuracy; it does not claim that unobserved intervals had no higher usage. Cumulative availability is independent. The controlled witness checks mixed exact and estimated values and a later unavailable current reading without substituting zero.

**Amendment (Body-bound class decisions)** · `amend:observe:semantic-classes` Refines (`amend:observe:coverage-admission`): the operation register records seven reviewer-confirmed semantic classes, their premises and named labelled operations. Each body binds to a class decision and an item-specific premise, alongside its existing separate full-recording, secret-flow and exposure assessments. Exceptions name the class and actual enclosing operation set; const, bootstrap and observation-internal exceptions remain distinct from structural value-trait inheritance. New payload representation, resource qualification and protected configuration bodies carry their additional premises locally. Mechanical checks reject missing class decisions or enclosing operation sets and changed bodies or types; they do not turn these semantic decisions into parser proofs.

**Amendment (Current carrier authority)** · `amend:observe:carrier-authority` Updates the Python-exhibition clause of (`amend:observe:foundation-evidence`) under (`amend:testing:python-carrier-adoption`): Python claim names in the evidence paragraphs are now ordinary citations resolved by the deployed linter, while the evidence join retains site/result, scoped-premise and bidirectional obligation checks. The complete locked transitive dependency review for (`amend:observe:export-dependencies`) is (`amend:observe:transitive-review`); inactive target branches remain reviewed without being claimed as host execution evidence.

**Amendment (Emission levels)** · `amend:observe:emission-levels` Clarifies (`amend:observe:full-content`), (`rule:observe:privacy`) and (`dec:observe:sinks`): full content is an instrumentation capability, while emission and persistence follow the selected level. Every labelled operation is counted and timed at every level under (`rule:observe:sampling`), including nested work; only public payload construction and emission depend on trace. Default summaries list observed series and the count of declared-but-unobserved series; trace retains the full declared roster. With PN_OBSERVE_LEVEL unset or set to default, the executable emits WARN and ERROR diagnostics, command completion metering with monotonic duration in seconds, outcome and totals, metric summaries, and a final observation-status record. Per-operation public payloads are not formatted or persisted at that level. PN_OBSERVE_LEVEL=trace enables complete compact-encoded span and operation content, including content-addressed objects under (`amend:observe:compact-content`); an unknown level is refused by name by the bootstrap. Secret roles and markers are unchanged at every level. Legacy debug and default-level arguments do not silently opt into persistence; RUST_LOG remains available to the separate directive-selection utility, not this bootstrap. Final per-process status reports successful delivery and whole-record loss before that status, excluding the status itself from delivered counts. Queue, sink and export failures never change binding results. The gate explicitly selects default, retains diagnostics inline and reports warning, error and loss counts per step. Controlled comparisons run disabled, default, trace and trace with local exporter failure against identical stdout and exit; the service-dependent remainder is unchanged.

**Amendment (Accounting and representation closure)** · `amend:observe:accounting-representation-closure` Under (`rule:observe:sampling`), every labelled operation retains identity-only accounting at default, with public payload construction deferred until trace. A raw outer Err constructor determines error outcome before structural Debug parsing, including payloads requiring custom fallback. The secret marker has a distinct representation tag from a public string. Content-addressed artifacts are synced before publication; a mismatched object is repaired by atomic replacement from a fresh synced temporary file, and the artifact root is made absolute at bootstrap. Bootstrap and export initialization expose typed configuration refusals separately from nonbinding availability; no initialization helper discards that distinction. Exception classes declare the complete set of their owner's labelled boundaries, including registry acquisition and its CDDL parsing, rather than pretending the class list is an item-specific call graph. Source-bound reviews and negative fixtures remain required; this class decision does not assert mechanical proof of secret flow.

**Amendment (Outcome and registry derivation)** · `amend:observe:outcome-and-registry-derivation` Under (`rule:observe:sampling`), default and trace use the same terminal outcome vocabulary: bounded return-constructor classification retains success or error without constructing a result payload at default; cancellation and unwinding retain their existing paths. Default return and execwrap byte-construction witnesses exercise these boundaries at their test sites. The compact observation register retains class membership rules, per-item justifications and source-bound semantic reviews; the gate derives class, exception and generator operation lists from the parsed build census and checks exact completeness, not subset membership. Expanded data is an untracked gate artifact. Controlled process witnesses rendezvous on final status or reader completion, tolerate diagnostic text, and enforce a separate generous fixture deadline that reports failure rather than wedging verification; it is not a performance-budget verdict.

**Amendment (Traced-child delivery evidence)** · `amend:observe:traced-child-delivery` Refines (`amend:observe:outcome-and-registry-derivation`): every captured child completion prints its final delivered and lost counts on the witness line and contributes them to the enclosing step's process counts. At trace, delivered records equal the captured JSON rows less the final status row. A nonzero trace loss appends an observation-completeness finding through the performance reporter with the original command outcome and no verdict effect; it never changes that outcome. Injected rendezvous fixtures identify themselves as injected and do not impersonate real process delivery or deaths. The development-only payload counter now lives at public_bytes itself, so a direct eager call is visible even if a caller bypasses an intermediate helper. The storage statement witness resets only its dedicated fixture tables before starting observation on every child invocation; a retake therefore exercises first-open catalogue, creation and identity statements again rather than inheriting a prior capture's initialized store. Complete-content acquisition selects the evidence sink and runs once: unexpected loss refuses distinctly from absent content. Only a control that injects loss may request up to {{ numval('num:numbers:observe-storage-capture-attempt-limit') }} attempts, with delivered private content and completed public results checked before retaking. A deterministic control discards one captured record after validating the original child content, identifies the resulting accounting as injected, retains its synthetic completeness finding separately, and requires the real retake to contain all fourteen statements. Real child accounting and any real loss findings remain separately witnessed; the control creates no node load.

**Amendment (Records contract instruments)** · `amend:observe:records-instruments` Implements the current pn-records operations of (`model:design:observation-map`) under (`conv:observe:metrics`). The stem records__root__sig__design__records owns validated_records, resolved_references and refusals counters in count units, summed across calls; active_validation is a concurrent-operation gauge; live_carrier_bytes is an estimated gauge of inline candidate bytes in active validation, excluding heap storage, accepted history and declarations; input_bytes records that same explicitly partial estimate once per validation call. No measurement controls a result. records_per_boundary observes the number of whole proposed acts in the assembled closure union, in count units. The common inclusive elapsed_seconds histogram and finite outcome series remain. The seven additional instruments have no attributes and belong only to the named RECORDS stem, independently of roster order. The runtime witness checks success and refusal counts at default and trace, zero lost updates, zero remaining active gauge values, unchanged stdout and exit, and full public operation content at trace.

**Amendment (Refusal outcomes)** · `amend:observe:refusal-outcomes` Refines (`rec:observe:decision`): refusal means a contract-mandated rejection in every crate; error means a failure. A boundary explicitly emits its bounded refusal outcome when rejecting its input. Explicit bounded outcomes take precedence over return-value inference across events, at default and trace alike. An Err return without an explicit contract outcome remains an error; neither classification changes the returned value or command verdict. For bounded-prefix decoding, refusal classifies the requested read; truncated input still requests more bytes and does not reject a document.

**Amendment (Records operation series)** · `amend:observe:records-operation-series` Refines (`amend:observe:records-instruments`) and (`conv:observe:metrics`): the RECORDS started_operations and completed_operations series have a bounded operation attribute whose vocabulary is derived from the checked operation registry. The generated Rust declaration is checked as a fixed point; unknown values cannot allocate a series and count as lost updates. Other owners retain their existing series. Assembly records records_per_boundary as the number of distinct whole proposed acts in the closure union, excluding fixed history. Default and trace witnesses assert each operation distribution, refusal distinct from error, the histogram and unchanged command results. The partial inline validation-byte estimate retains its stated exclusions.

**Amendment (Delivery causes and exit disclosure)** · `amend:observe:delivery-cause-and-exit` Refines (`amend:observe:compact-content`) and (`rule:observe:sampling`). The ordinary queue retains structured values with a serialized byte charge instead of decoding its own JSON again; the former decode boundary lost deeply nested public payloads. Content-addressed chunks also bound inline JSON nesting to {{ numval('num:numbers:observe-inline-nesting-level-count') }} levels, preserving complete content and ordinary-reader compatibility. Each final status names queue-full, byte-charge, record-size, capture-overflow, span-depth, reserved-channel-full, recursive-observation, artifact and writer losses separately. The exit drain allowance is {{ numval('num:numbers:observe-drain-base-seconds') }} second plus {{ numval('num:numbers:observe-drain-per-mib-seconds') }} second per queued MiB rounded up, capped at {{ numval('num:numbers:observe-drain-maximum-seconds') }} seconds by the existing {{ numval('num:numbers:observe-queued-byte-capacity') }} bytes charge bound. After that wait, a synchronous final status reports attempted, delivered, lost, in_flight_records and queued-undelivered records as disjoint counts. At most one publication reserved before the cutoff is in flight; captured records excluding the status lie between completed delivery and completed delivery plus that reservation. Reservation precedes acquisition of the transport write lock, so the reserved write can land before or after status, or remain incomplete at process exit; the capture interval does not assert its completion. A second closing check after compaction forbids unreserved publication past the cutoff. No reader rendezvous is required for exit disclosure. The delivery worker stops taking new records at that cutoff. Publication holds no accounting lock across transport I/O, so waiting for an in-flight write shares the drain deadline. The shipped records and synchronous final status share stderr and its write lock; the final status can therefore wait for the same stalled transport. Its write itself may block; no completion is claimed after process death. Injected deadlines establish the tail-disclosure contract without sleeps or widened test margins.

**Amendment (Records access and assembly accounting)** · `amend:observe:records-field-inheritance` Refines (`amend:observe:records-instruments`) and (`amend:observe:records-operation-series`). Seventeen pure immutable field accessors inherit the labelled operation that supplied their validated view; repeated field reads create neither spans nor invocations. Complete-act-access remains the act-level validated batch access. Assembly increments the separate assembly_steps counter, in count units, for root visits, parent inspections, inherited-member insertion attempts and emitted members. The common work_operations counter remains exactly one per invoked operation. The eighth records-only instrument has no attributes; other owners' series are unchanged. The checked runtime witness reads every accessor repeatedly, asserts the exact operation distribution and separately checks assembly work.

**Amendment (Trace burst capacity)** · `amend:observe:trace-burst-capacity` The ordinary non-blocking delivery channel admits at most {{ numval('num:numbers:observe-queue-record-capacity') }} records and retains the independent {{ numval('num:numbers:observe-queued-byte-capacity') }} bytes queued-byte bound; reserved summary and diagnostic channels remain separate. A burst witness with {{ row('org.peer-network.observe.fixtures', name='trace-burst').number_forms.ordinary_records | display }} ordinary records and its reserved summary stalls the writer throughout production, then releases it by rendezvous and requires {{ numval('num:numbers:observe-burst-delivered-record-count') }} delivered with zero lost. This admits short trace bursts without a timing margin or blocking computation; larger or oversized bursts may still lose records and must report that loss. The direct witness [ordinary_queue_overflow](../packages/cli-common/src/observation/tests.rs) holds the writer by rendezvous, exceeds the ordinary slot capacity, and requires precisely the excess as queue-full loss, with delivered plus lost equal to attempted. The locked workspace interchange example measures the real burst separately, and its loss remains a nonverdict finding under (`rule:observe:sampling`). Complete-trace evidence fixtures select a separate bounded configuration only through the existing observation-test-hook feature: PN_OBSERVE_COMPLETE_EVIDENCE admits at most {{ row('org.peer-network.observe.fixtures', name='complete-evidence').number_forms.ordinary_records | display }} ordinary records with the unchanged {{ numval('num:numbers:observe-queued-byte-capacity') }} bytes queued-byte and per-record bounds. Host storage, secured-service, sensitive and binary-row controls, the failing-export workload and document checks select this same evidence configuration. Every complete capture prints its total attempted records beside the ordinary-slot bound and refuses excess before content assertions; count